From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:07:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: add the SGHD instruction set (STEINS;GATE Steam)

TYN-only. The Steam release of STEINS;GATE (2016) speaks the Chaos;Child PC dialect of the SC3 virtual
machine: the system/graphics/user tables agree in about two thirds of the opcodes by operand shape, and the
ScrWork layout is the CC one (the startup script fades through GlobalVars 4400/4401/4402 = SW_MASK1COLOR/
ALPHA/PRI, SW_MESMODE0 = 4363, SW_SAVEERRORCODE = 3333). Running the 190 scripts against a reference
disassembly (instruction lengths of every executed opcode compared with an independent decoder: ~230,000
instructions from boot through the first scene) shows no other operand mismatch than the ones fixed here.

Add InstructionSet::SGHD. opcodetables_sghd.h starts from copies of the CC tables and overrides the opcodes
that differ (inst_sghd.h, header only like the tables):
  - 00:4C   type byte, one expression when the type is 0 (CC: Dummy)
  - 10:1B, 10:3F  one byte, no known effect (CC: Dummy, which hangs the thread: the startup script executes
            10:3F before the title)
  - 10:37   phone/mail group (CC: MapSystem): type byte and per-type operands, stubbed
  - 10:38   type byte, a label when the type is 0 (CC: Mtrg), stubbed
Every GameInstructionSet == CC site that applies is extended: SelInit savepoint id, NameID name plate label,
Tips data init (two labels), MSinit memset sizes, the CC title menu state machine (press-to-start check), and
the three background tint reads. ReportsSaveErrors() is deliberately not extended; until an S;G save system
exists SaveSystem::LoadSystemData reports OK for SGHD (the startup script treats Failed as fatal).

